# Local helper docs, internal reports and temp scripts.
# These are working notes, not repository content: they are kept on the
# maintainer's disk and deliberately never published. Listing them here is not
# on its own enough -- a rule added after a file is already tracked does
# nothing, which is how twenty release notes and AGENTS.md stayed in the tree
# long after this section claimed to exclude them. Untrack with
# `git rm --cached`, never `git add -f`.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
code-review-report-*.html
*-report.html
scripts/
spm.sh.*.bk
test-*.csv
test.md

# Local agent state and machine-local backups. These are large, private, and
# have no business in a release; the ignore rules did not previously stop an
# accidental `git add`.
.nexus/
SansBACKUP_DEC_25/
